  f(f(f(f(f(X, V), f(f(X, X), f(f(X, X), f(V, V)))), f(X, X)), f(Y, f(Y, f(f(X, X), f(X, X))))), f(f(f(X, V), f(f(X, X), f(f(X, X), f(V, V)))), f(f(X, V), f(f(X, X), f(f(X, X), f(V, V))))))
= { by axiom 1 (hyp) R->L }
  Y

Lemma 28: f(X, Y) = X.
Proof:
  f(X, Y)
= { by lemma 24 R->L }
